    "priceSource": "fallback",
    "idsName": "261640",
    "idsInfo": "65894",
    "info": "ENGINE COMPONENTS\nFusion engines generate thrust by superheating plasma in a magnetic bottle. The plasma is then emitted as exhaust through a nozzle assembly, providing thrust for even the largest of battleships. The temperatures and pressures exerted by a fusion engine require that their components be manufactured from High-Temperature Alloys, while Superconductors are necessary to generate the huge magnetic fields needed to contain the plasma.",
