    "price": 500,
    "itemIcon": "",
    "combinable": false,
    "priceSource": "fallback",
    "idsName": "261618",
    "idsInfo": "65897",
    "info": "OXYGEN\nA typical human being consumes over 12,000 liters of Oxygen (O2) daily. Oxygen, usually mixed with a neutral gas such as nitrogen, is absorbed through the tissues of the lungs and then diffused into the bloodstream, where it is carried throughout the body. All humans require a constant supply of Oxygen or they will perish within minutes.",
